names(trees) = c("a", "b")
class(trees) <- "multiPhylo"

And try to plot with a color variable

ggtree(trees, aes(color=estimate_extrinsic))  %<+% dd_all  + facet_wrap(~.id, scale="free") + geom_tiplab()

With a data frame with a column ".id" to map the variable

# A tibble: 72 x 4 taxa name estimate_extrinsic .id <chr> <chr> <dbl> <fct>  1 Root TME -0.632 a  2 Epi epithelial -0.358 a  3 Endo endothelial 0.0980 a  4 Fibro fibroblast -0.322 a  5 Adipo adipocyte -0.928 a  6 Immune immune_cell -0.291 a  7 Granulo granulocyte -0.413 a  8 Eosin eosinophil 1.76 a  9 Neutro neutrophil 1.53 a 10 Mono deriv mono_derived -0.865 a # ... with 62 more rows

